   ],
   "mechanisms_outside_ir": [
    {
     "mechanism": "Attention logit soft-capping inside every attention layer: the pre-softmax scores are replaced by 50*tanh(scores/50). The IR attention op has no hook for transforming its scores.",
     "quote": "$$\\text{logits} \\leftarrow \\text{soft\\_cap} * \\tanh(\\text{logits} / \\text{soft\\_cap}).$$\nWe set the soft\\_cap parameter to $50.0$ for the self-attention layers and to $30.0$ for the final layer.",
     "where": "Sec. Model Architecture"
    },
    {
     "mechanism": "Layer-alternating attention type: local sliding window (4096) and global attention (8192 span) alternate every other layer, so blocks are not identical.",
     "quote": "We alternate between a local sliding window attention~\\citep{slidingwindow, beltagy2020longformer} and global attention~\\citep{globalattention} in every other layer.",
     "where": "Sec. Model Architecture"
    }
   ],
   "notes": "All three released sizes are described; primary is 2B, and the block attributes use 2B values. The attention op shows the local layers (window 4096). Global layers use window 0 within the 8192 context, and the paper does not say which layer parity is local. The table's 'Feedforward dim' is reported as stated (18432 for 2B). It may count the gate and up projections together; the paper does not clarify. 'Approximated GeGLU' does not name the approximation, so gelu approx is left not_stated. Left not_stated: RMSNorm eps, RoPE theta/pairing/fraction, attention scale, biases, embedding scaling, and whether there is a final norm before the head (none is described, so none is included). The residual adds rest on the cited Vaswani transformer architecture. The MHA, wide and smaller-window variants are ablations and are not described."
  },
